agent: A current implementation already exists: Northwind Restock Alerts.
  **Here is a proposed starting point for your implementation:**
  **Title:** Use Scheduled Pipeline
  **Summary:** A GitHub Actions scheduled workflow runs every Monday, queries stock levels and reorder points from the order service with a read-only token, and emails one restock alert to the warehouse lead. It is not running yet.
  **Realizations:**
  - **Scheduler:** GitHub Actions scheduled workflow; starts the job each Monday.
  - **Stock reader:** Order service stock query with a read-only token; reads stock levels without writing.
  - **Alert sender:** Email to the warehouse lead; sends one alert listing items at or below their reorder point.
  **Deployment:** A scheduled GitHub Actions workflow on a hosted runner.
  **Data:** Stock levels and reorder points move from the order service to the workflow and are not stored.
  **Security:** The stock credential is read-only and stored in repository secrets. Payment data is not read.
  **Operations:** The workflow depends on the order service’s monthly availability target. Failed runs may go unnoticed until someone checks the workflow.
  **Deployed by:** GitHub Actions.
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will use GitHub Actions to get Use Scheduled Pipeline up and running.
  **Managed by:** GitHub Actions.
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will use GitHub Actions for managing Use Scheduled Pipeline once it’s running.
  **Language:** None.
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will treat this as a Platform to manage as opposed to a coding project to write.
  **Capabilities:**
  - **Weekly restock alert:** Realized by GitHub Actions.
  - **Reorder point check:** Realized by the order service stock query.
